"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC bob-cli-ra[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Tree-note link walks[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]On area, project, notebook, and prose notes, `\\[n` / `]n` step [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]through the note's same-type siblings under its parent (wrapping), [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and `[N` / `]N` tour that type's parents in outline order. Every [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Property Card ends with the link-walk rail, below all cabinets. [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Keys, repeats, the links footer, and the rail always agree. Nothing[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]is written to the vault, and none of it races the bob-cli-qq [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]cabinets go-live.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]6[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]tree_note_link_walks.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/tree_note_link_walks.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-ra[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-ra/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Sibling-ring engine and the tree route in api.navGroups[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]engine[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]engine: add the cross-epic gate edges, then build the lazy, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]generation-stamped tree index and the derived `tree` route in Bob Ledger[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Tools' api.navGroups (membership, catalog-order comparators, project [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lanes, the outline-order parent tour, exists-only stops, and explicit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]none reasons), with parity vectors and a perf test.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Matcher hardening, key notices, and the links footer copy[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]nav[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav: stop matching step links inside inline code, count authored step [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]links only on nav lines on tree routes, pass the tree fields through [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolveNavLinks and walkMode.links, give `\\[n`/`]n`/`[N`/`]N` useful [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notices, and teach the `n` walker-footer panel parents, lanes, wraps, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and singletons.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rail kit polish, the card-floor helper, and the tree rail [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]adapter[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]rail[dim] · [dim][/dim]after engine[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rail: add the kit's card-floor helpers, step-item wrap and tooltip [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]support, and the pure tree rail model plus its activation, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-validation, and live-refresh mixin, all unit-tested and previewed. No[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]card mounts it yet.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]The rail on every tree card and the card-floor invariant[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cards[dim] · [dim][/dim]after nav, rail[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cards: after bob-cli-qq.10.5 closes, mount the rail on area, project, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notebook, and prose cards in both views, make the foot and cabinet stack[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]insert above the floor, move the day/period and record rails to the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]floor, and prove that any rail is the card's last child on every [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]species.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Real-Obsidian link-walk acceptance with screenshot review[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]acceptance[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cards[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]acceptance: add a scratch-vault runner for all eight keys on all four [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]types, check that rail, footer, and keys agree, run the floor, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]passivity, console-error, and perf checks plus re-validation, review [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every screenshot on athena, and reach GO.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plugin docs, the link-walk glossary term, and approved memory[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after acceptance[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: after bob-cli-qq.10.6 closes, document the tree route, the walk [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rules, and the rail-as-floor contract in the bob-plugins docs. Then [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]write the approved memory (the link-walk strand, the walker-footer [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]correction, and any approved extras), regenerate, and pass both docs [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]gates.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-ra","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-ra.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-79ef64f8b026ec5e320ddb77fb793cc2","started_at":"2026-11-27T20:03:17.514830+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"9a988b78c7c40ec218cd382e7b1d520b7c27c75446b50ab78ef62bdfe28184b2","path":"agents/bbugyi200.apollo.bob-cli-ra.2--pla